    "long_instructions": "# Update Objects using Dot and Bracket Notation\r\n\r\n1. **Prompt**\r\n   Ask AI how to update object properties using dot notation and bracket notation.\r\n\r\n2. **Analyze**\r\n   Examine the AI’s examples, noting the similarities and differences between the two methods.\r\n\r\n3. **Integrate**\r\n   Try both methods to change property values in your object by writing the following functions:\r\n   * `renameDessert`: Change `dessert.name` to `\"Cookie Sundae\"` (use dot notation).\r\n   * `toggleFrozen`: Write an if/else statement to flip the `isFrozen` boolean.\r\n   * `recategorizeFlavor`: Create a variable `key = \"flavor\"` and use bracket notation to change the value to `\"Peanut Butter\"`.\r\n   * **Important**: After writing your 3 functions, wire them to the matching buttons (`#rename`, `#toggle-frozen`, `#recategorize`) so they run when clicked. Don't forget to call `render()` inside each function.\r\n\r\n4. **Reflect**\r\n   Which syntax feels easier or clearer? When might you need bracket notation instead?",
